{% doc %}
  Breadcrumb trail and its BreadcrumbList JSON-LD, built once from the same
  data so they can never disagree. This is the ONLY place a BreadcrumbList is
  emitted; do not add another.

  Rules (Google and WCAG):
  - The trail reflects a stable site hierarchy, not the visitor's click path.
  - Product: product metafield singi.primary_collection, else the collection the
    visitor came from, else the product's first collection in Shopify's order (never
    "all" or "frontpage"), else just Home > Product. So a direct visit to a product
    still shows where it lives.
  - Collection and product ancestors come from the collection metafield
    singi.parent_collection, up to three levels, and, when a collection has none,
    from where the collection sits in the breadcrumb menu (theme setting
    Navigation > Breadcrumb menu, default main-menu). Metafields win over the menu.
    Pages, blogs and the collections list use the menu the same way (they have no
    metafield); an article uses its blog's place in the menu, then the blog, then itself.
    Define both metafields with `npm run seo:metafields`.
  - Absolute URLs in JSON-LD; the last JSON-LD item is the current page, which is not a link and
    is not drawn in the visible trail (the heading already says it).
  - The visible trail is drawn only when there is at least one ancestor besides the
    current page. A lone current page adds nothing the heading does not, so the
    nav is omitted (the JSON-LD still lists Home and the page). Sections then get
    their normal top padding, because the breadcrumb spacing rule needs the nav.
  - Home is in the JSON-LD but not in the visible trail (saves space).
  - Semantic nav > ol > li, separators drawn by CSS.

  @param {string} kind - product, collection, collections, article, blog or page

  @example
  {% render 'breadcrumbs', kind: 'product' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign origin = request.origin
  assign titles = ''
  assign urls = ''
  assign start = blank
  assign current_title = ''
  assign current_url = ''

  case kind
    when 'product'
      assign current_title = product.title
      assign current_url = product.url
      assign start = product.metafields.singi.primary_collection.value
      if start == blank and collection != blank and collection.handle != 'all' and collection.handle != 'frontpage'
        assign start = collection
      endif
      if start == blank
        for candidate in product.collections
          if candidate.handle != 'all' and candidate.handle != 'frontpage'
            assign start = candidate
            break
          endif
        endfor
      endif
      if start != blank
        assign titles = start.title | append: '||'
        assign urls = start.url | append: '||'
      endif
    when 'collection'
      assign current_title = collection.title
      assign current_url = collection.url
      assign start = collection
    when 'collections'
      assign current_title = 'collections.title' | t
      assign current_url = routes.collections_url
    when 'article'
      assign current_title = article.title
      assign current_url = article.url
      assign titles = blog.title | append: '||'
      assign urls = blog.url | append: '||'
    when 'blog'
      assign current_title = blog.title
      assign current_url = blog.url
    when 'page'
      assign current_title = page.title
      assign current_url = page.url
  endcase

  assign metafield_parents = 0
  if start != blank
    assign node = start
    for step in (1..3)
      assign parent = node.metafields.singi.parent_collection.value
      if parent == blank
        break
      endif
      assign metafield_parents = metafield_parents | plus: 1
      assign titles = parent.title | append: '||' | append: titles
      assign urls = parent.url | append: '||' | append: urls
      assign node = parent
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    No metafield parents: look the page up in the breadcrumb menu. Its parents in the menu
    (one or two levels, menus nest three deep) become its ancestors. Liquid cannot recurse, so the
    levels are unrolled, and `found` stops the outer loops. Parents that point at "all", the
    front page or nowhere are skipped, they are not useful steps.
  endcomment
  comment
    The page whose place in the menu is looked up: a collection (also a product's), a page, a blog,
    the collections list, or, for an article, its blog (the article itself is never in a menu).
  endcomment
  assign target = blank
  case kind
    when 'product', 'collection'
      if start != blank
        assign target = start.url
      endif
    when 'article'
      assign target = blog.url
    else
      assign target = current_url
  endcase

  if target != blank and metafield_parents == 0 and settings.breadcrumb_menu != blank
    assign menu = linklists[settings.breadcrumb_menu]
    assign found = false
    assign menu_titles = ''
    assign menu_urls = ''
    for first in menu.links
      if found
        break
      endif
      if first.url == target
        break
      endif
      for second in first.links
        if found
          break
        endif
        if second.url == target
          assign found = true
          assign menu_titles = first.title | append: '||'
          assign menu_urls = first.url | append: '||'
          break
        endif
        for third in second.links
          if third.url == target
            assign found = true
            assign menu_titles = first.title | append: '||' | append: second.title | append: '||'
            assign menu_urls = first.url | append: '||' | append: second.url | append: '||'
            break
          endif
        endfor
      endfor
    endfor
    if found
      assign menu_title_list = menu_titles | split: '||'
      assign menu_url_list = menu_urls | split: '||'
      assign kept_titles = ''
      assign kept_urls = ''
      for menu_title in menu_title_list
        assign menu_url = menu_url_list[forloop.index0]
        assign menu_handle = menu_url | split: '/' | last
        if menu_url == blank or menu_url == '#' or menu_url == routes.root_url or menu_handle == 'all' or menu_handle == 'frontpage'
          continue
        endif
        assign kept_titles = kept_titles | append: menu_title | append: '||'
        assign kept_urls = kept_urls | append: menu_url | append: '||'
      endfor
      assign titles = kept_titles | append: titles
      assign urls = kept_urls | append: urls
    endif
  endif

  assign title_list = titles | split: '||'
  assign url_list = urls | split: '||'
  assign trail_id = canonical_url | default: origin | append: current_url
-%}

{%- comment -%} A trail of only the current page says nothing the heading does not, so it is not drawn. The JSON-LD below is still complete. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ancestors = titles | remove: '||' | strip -%}
{%- if ancestors != blank -%}
  <nav class="breadcrumbs eyebrow" aria-label="{{ 'general.breadcrumbs' | t }}">
    <ol role="list">
      {%- for title in title_list -%}
        {%- if title != blank -%}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ url_list[forloop.index0] }}">{{ title | escape }}</a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ol>
  </nav>
{%- endif -%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "@id": {{ trail_id | append: '#breadcrumb' | json }},
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": {{ 'general.home' | t | json }},
        "item": {{ origin | append: routes.root_url | json }}
      }
      {%- assign position = 1 -%}
      {%- for title in title_list -%}
        {%- if title != blank -%}
          {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
          ,
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ position }},
            "name": {{ title | json }},
            "item": {{ origin | append: url_list[forloop.index0] | json }}
          }
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
      ,
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": {{ position }},
        "name": {{ current_title | json }},
        "item": {{ origin | append: current_url | json }}
      }
    ]
  }
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* One line, never wraps. The last ancestor truncates; the others keep their full width and the trail clips rather than scrolls the page.
     Truncation is visual: the full text stays in the DOM for screen readers and the h1 shows it in full. */
  /* Spacing follows the 1rem base unit (docs/design-system.md). The trail's 2.75rem line box already puts
     about 1rem of air above and below its 12px text, so it adds no padding or margin of its own: the header
     is the space above, and whatever follows starts right after the line box. */
  .section:has(> .breadcrumbs) { padding-block-start: 0; }
  .section > .breadcrumbs + * { margin-block-start: 0; }
  .breadcrumbs { overflow: hidden; }
  .breadcrumbs ol { display: flex; flex-wrap: nowrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .breadcrumbs li { display: flex; align-items: center; flex: none; }
  .breadcrumbs li:last-child { flex: 0 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
  .breadcrumbs li + li::before { content: '/'; flex: none; margin-inline-end: 0.5rem; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .breadcrumbs a { display: block; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; line-height: 2.75rem; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  .breadcrumbs a { text-decoration: none; }
  .breadcrumbs a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
{% endstylesheet %}
